{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nThis reconciler-test cohort contains 44 confirmed bloated prose blocks across exactly 8 file-impact paths. Condense repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, and obsolete history while retaining current non-obvious contracts.\n\nThe inventory and before-citations are pinned to `origin/main@dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d`. The 8 original paths were renamed into `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing`; Git recognizes each rename at 87–99% similarity. All 44 named docstrings remain present at the current basis. Use dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d as the immutable before side. In a grouped commit, verify this leaf by filtering `dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d..HEAD` to its 8 declared paths; a separate batch check verifies the full changed-path union.\n\n## Editing boundary and semantic guard\nEdit only allowlisted comments/docstrings plus adjacent blank lines. Executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose stay unchanged. Rewrite stale RED/pre-fix language as current contracts.\n\nFor every path, parse immutable and final source with `ast.parse(source, type_comments=True)`; recursively strip only a leading `Expr(Constant(str))` from each `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, and `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require exact `ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False)` equality. A tokenizer guard separately preserves directive text/attachment; runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n\n## Scope — 44 editable blocks\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_differ_rebar_id_exclusion.py` (2) — module and test_outbound_differ_excludes_colon_form_rebar_id_label docstrings. Preserve colon-form bridge-label exclusion without masking real outbound differences.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_effective_map_cache_d378.py` (1) — module docstring beginning “Per-project effective-map memoization…”. Preserve one discovery per distinct project, project-keyed mapping, and unchanged create output.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_parent_clear_bidirectional_37e7.py` (9) — module; _FakeBindingStore, _local_tickets, _remote_fields, _snapshot, and _run_outbound docstrings; all three test docstrings. Preserve real inbound/outbound composition, peer-parent evidence, remote de-parenting, suppression of peer removals, local re-set propagation, and final inbound clear.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_parent_clear_requires_peer_evidence.py` (6) — module, _FakeBindingStore, and _child docstrings; docstrings of test_a_parent_the_peer_never_had_is_not_cleared, test_a_parent_the_peer_once_had_is_cleared, and test_an_unobserved_parent_is_never_cleared_even_with_peer_evidence. Preserve positive peer evidence, observed-empty versus unobserved parent state, local-only parent safety, and legitimate clear behavior.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_parent_detach_sync.py` (2) — module and test_unmanaged_jira_parent_is_not_cleared docstrings. Preserve managed-ref-gated detach propagation and protection of human-managed Jira parents.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_parent_drop_parity_8390.py` (11) — module, _tickets, _alert_kinds, and _update_drop docstrings; docstrings of the bound-drop, unbound-control, epic-parent, no-sink, ACLI-400-recording, ACLI-400-swallowing, and converged-vs-dropped tests. Preserve create/update parity, bound versus unbound/epic parents, durable divergence alerts, optional sinks, 400-only soft failure, and unchanged convergence discrimination.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_parent_emit_suppression_is_loud_9f26.py` (8) — module and _remote docstrings; docstrings of the suppressed, already-converged, divergent, unbound-non-epic, epic-parent, and bridge-alert-store tests. Preserve operator-visible suppression only for real dropped fields, negative controls, accepted parent emission, optional observability, and end-to-end alert persistence.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py` (5) — module docstring; docstrings of test_a_converged_pair_plans_no_outbound_update_after_our_own_write, test_a_key_that_left_the_fetch_window_plans_no_outbound_create, test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create, and test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression. Preserve stale-local-state suppression, non-vacuous differ preconditions, departed-window safety, genuine inbound creates, and invariant seed preservation.\n\n## Consumers and protected directives\nPytest directly collects every impacted module; `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is the deterministic prose-policy consumer. No targeted `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or doctest consumer was found. Six protected directive tokens: # type: ignore[union-attr] in outbound_rebar_id, parent_detach, parent_drop, and parent_emit_suppression; snapshot_stale_local_state also has that token and # pragma: no cover - import bootstrap. Preserve each complete directive token and its attached executable statement exactly.\n\n## Independent review receipt\nA reviewer who did not author the prose change must post exactly 44 leaf-linked TSV rows, one per edited block:\n`path<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session`\n\nBoth verdicts are `PASS`, citations use full SHAs, and every after count is lower. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the 44 allowlisted prose blocks or adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and states only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints.\n- [ ] Normalized AST dumps are exactly equal between dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d and final `HEAD`.\n- [ ] Protected directive text and attachment are exact; runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n- [ ] Sorted paths changed by `dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d..HEAD` within this leaf's declared paths exactly equal all 8 file-impact paths.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV has exactly 44 passing rows with full before/final SHAs.\n- [ ] Path-scoped diff integrity, comment hygiene, and pytest over every impacted file pass.\n- [ ] Worktree-venv `make verify` passes without a timeout.\n\n## Verification\nRun all seven structured commands: `semantic`, `directives`, `paths`, `diff`, `hygiene`, `focused`, and `full`. Executable guards prove behavior/directive/path preservation; the TSV decides each block’s semantic preservation and bloat removal."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792719536336649158,"uuid":"cae47cb9-aeab-44d3-be99-fd949faad0c7"}